invalid type: string "CHAPTER 12 : SYNCHRONIZATION TOOLS\nSemaphores, Mutexes, Monitors & Classic Problems\nCounting Semaphores, Monitors, and Classic Synchronization Challenges\n12.1 MUTEX LOCKS VS. COUNTING SEMAPHORES\nWhile spinlocks waste CPU cycles in busy-waiting loops, higher-level primitives put waiting threads to sleep until the resource\nbecomes available:\nMutex (Mutual Exclusion Lock)ÿ